> Which contract page declares which rule tags, and where to fetch each one.
> run.sh reads this to name the pages a run needed and did not have.
>
>   <tag prefix>  <file under the contracts directory>  <where it comes from>
>
> The pages are not copied into this directory on purpose: a normative page
> living in two public repositories is a reader who cannot tell which one binds
> them. This file is the pointer, and a pointer is not a second copy.

DL     download.md  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openabstractions/abstraction-download/main/CONTRACT.md
ID     identity.md  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openabstractions/abstraction-identity/main/CONTRACT.md
JOB    job.md       https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openabstractions/abstraction-job/main/CONTRACT.md
LOG    logging.md   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openabstractions/abstraction-logging/main/CONTRACT.md
WATCH  watch.md     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openabstractions/abstraction-watch/main/README.md
